From 691ffcc4858f707364245aa96f720a87dce4a55c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 06:13:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix PostHog: live key pointed at a nonexistent project (401
 on every event)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The snippet in client/index.html and the Vite env default both carried
a stale phc_ token that PostHog rejects with 401 — zero events or session
replays were ever ingested. Replace with the real project token (public
client key by design). Also allow GA4 regional collect endpoints
(*.google-analytics.com / *.analytics.google.com) in the CSP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ChWFzYUmmKjCBD1YWCdhQY
